	(text "K-10 DECIDED (fail-off): 4.7 k pull-down on the enable, main MCU drives it through 1 k, supervisor veto via one BSS138.\nOn Rev B the enable node is LM51551 UVLO/EN (FLY_EN). EN rising threshold 0.4-0.7 V, UVLO 1.425-1.575 V (SNVSB75E).\nMCU high: 3.3 V x 4.7/(4.7+1) = 2.72 V -> run.  Pull-down only: 0 V -> shutdown.  BSS138 on: ~0 V -> shutdown.\nVeto default (owner decision 10 Oct 2026, OPEN item 3 closed): R403 10k PULL-UP fitted -> veto ON whenever the supervisor\nis in reset, crashed with its pin high/high-Z, or not running; firmware must drive PB0 LOW to permit 48 V. (R404 removed.)\nPMD401 park (owner decision 10 Oct 2026, OPEN item 4): open-drain Q402 BSS138 with R405 10k gate PULL-UP -> AEN held LOW\n(parked) by default; the PMD401's own 22k pull-up provides the run level, so no 3.3/5 V level question. Supervisor drives\nPB1 (SUP_PARK) LOW to unpark. BSS138 VGS(th) 0.9-1.5 V (Nexperia BSS138P datasheet). SG-03/SG-05 still required on hardware."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 20 0)
